    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't think it's a phase though. it's not like i'm just 'shifting' or whatever. the person i was... they didn't just change, they died. and everything that's left is just this pathetic, empty shell. it's like trying to fix a computer that's been completely wiped. there's nothing to reconnect to. there's just nothing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that a core part of you has fundamentally passed away is a devastating kind of grief, and it's understandable why you feel so empty right now. When you feel like you've been wiped clean, the focus needs to shift from \"fixing\" the old person to gently acknowledging the reality of the *current* you. Even if nothing feels recognizable, the person who is reading this message is still here, and that is a starting point. Professional support can help you navigate this immense sense of loss and start discovering what can be built from the quiet space that remains.",
